KG42.register("source_edge_archive-37af65783df278793d975897",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E25","v141-b-g05-e07"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-259000fdd3b58453","target":"COMP-0f9c791362e86686","source_occurrence_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","source_unit_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Local allocation component of the utility-integrated model for Coalition {VIU, Private investor}, whose distribution constraints are also included in the grand-coalition model. | Local microgrid allocation model for Coalition {Private investor, D}. | Microgrid allocation optimization in Coalition {Private investor, D}, within the iterative utility–microgrid equilibrium calculation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g04-E12","v141-b-g04-E16","v141-b-g04-E21","v141-b-g04-E25","v141-b-g05-e07"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"3e37b5d78887d9e5002452193a0a994c64f054b980110679b08168c48c1e38d7","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Repeat regulated-price updates and consumers’ responses, with the models solved again for power dispatch, until convergence is achieved. Scope: Numerical equilibrium solution for Coalitions {VIU}, {D}, {VIU, D}, {VIU, Private investor} and {VIU, Private investor, D}. Repeat the separate utility–microgrid decision iteration, in which the microgrid updates its decisions in response to the resulting regulated utility price, until convergence is achieved. Scope: Numerical equilibrium solution for Coalition {Private investor, D}, with separate utility and microgrid optimization models. Regulators may introduce feed-in premiums on top of market prices to promote microgrid development and efficient operation, including higher production at peak hours. Scope: Proposed regulatory incentives for microgrid development and efficient operation.","target_definition":"The utility’s regulated price provides a coordination signal for the microgrid’s optimization of electricity generation, grid imports and reactive power production; the microgrid updates these decisions in response to the resulting regulated price. Scope: Microgrid allocation optimization in Coalition {Private investor, D}, within the iterative utility–microgrid equilibrium calculation. Condition: The utility and microgrid optimize separately; the microgrid treats the utility’s regulated price as fixed during each optimization step. Local allocations must satisfy Kirchhoff’s Current Law at distribution nodes and exclude microgrid exports to the main grid. Distribution expansion enters the microgrid model as a parameter determined by the utility. Scope: Local microgrid allocation model for Coalition {Private investor, D}. Condition: The utility is outside the coalition and determines distribution expansion in its own optimization problem. The allocation model permits generation at distribution nodes and power exports from the microgrid to the rest of the grid, subject to distribution-flow constraints. Scope: Local allocation component of the utility-integrated model for Coalition {VIU, Private investor}, whose distribution constraints are also included in the grand-coalition model. Condition: The microgrid is fully integrated with utility operations.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The utility’s regulated price provides a coordination signal for the microgrid’s optimization of electricity generation, grid imports and reactive power production; the microgrid updates these decisions in response to the resulting regulated price. Scope: Microgrid allocation optimization in Coalition {Private investor, D}, within the iterative utility–microgrid equilibrium calculation. Condition: The utility and microgrid optimize separately; the microgrid treats the utility’s regulated price as fixed during each optimization step.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E25","v141-b-g05-e07","v141-b-g05-e05","v141-b-g05-e08"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p17-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":17,"printed_page":"540","section":"Appendix C. Solution approach","anchor_text":"} { , , } g p [17 recover the utility’s costs only, since the private investor is not sub- ject to c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-17.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Solving Coalition {Private investor, D} introduces an additional complexity: the utility and the microgrid take decisions separately, but these decisions influence each other. Their optimization models are solved iteratively. In the first step, given an initial value for the utility’s regulated price, the microgrid optimizes electricity generation, imports from the main grid and reactive power production; the MG treats the utility’s regulated price as fixed. In the second step, the utility optimizes power dispatch in the network, given the microgrid’s quantity decisions; the VIU treats MG exports and generation as fixed. The microgrid successively updates its decisions based on the resulting regulated price for the utility. These steps are repeated until convergence is achieved. Searching for the equilibrium can still be thought of as solving a fixed point problem, where Q^{-1}(P) are the MG’s power imports from the microgrid’s problem. The regulated electricity price depends on Q, the total utility’s sales, that include the microgrid’s imports decisions (Q^{-1}(P)), as well as sales at the other nodes of the network."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g05-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p17-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":17,"printed_page":"540","section":"Appendix C. Solution approach","anchor_text":"} { , , } g p [17 recover the utility’s costs only, since the private investor is not sub- ject to c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-17.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Solving Coalition {Private investor, D} introduces an additional complexity: the utility and the microgrid take decisions separately, but these decisions influence each other. Their optimization models are solved iteratively. In the first step, given an initial value for the utility’s regulated price, the microgrid optimizes electricity generation, imports from the main grid and reactive power production; the MG treats the utility’s regulated price as fixed. In the second step, the utility optimizes power dispatch in the network, given the microgrid’s quantity decisions; the VIU treats MG exports and generation as fixed. The microgrid successively updates its decisions based on the resulting regulated price for the utility. These steps are repeated until convergence is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g05-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p17-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":17,"printed_page":"540","section":"Appendix C. Solution approach","anchor_text":"y g y q y sales (Eq. (3)). Thus, ﬁnding the equilibrium price and quantities is a ﬁxed point problem","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-17.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Our variable of interest is the regulated electricity price, $P(Q)$. Given a continuous function mapping of $P$ into itself, $P(Q(P))$, the objective is to find a price $P^*$ such that $P^* = P(Q(P^*))$ and we achieve convergence to a fixed point. Convergence is not guaranteed, even if this exists; however, if the procedure converges, it will be to a fixed point. This iterative approach to finding a fixed point equilibrium has worked well in our study."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g05-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p17-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":17,"printed_page":"540","section":"Appendix C. Solution approach","anchor_text":"} { , , } g p [17 recover the utility’s costs only, since the private investor is not sub- ject to c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-17.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Searching for the equilibrium can still be thought of as solving a fixed point problem, where $Q_1(P)$ are the MG’s power imports from the microgrid’s problem. The regulated electricity price depends on $Q$, the total utility’s sales, that include the microgrid’s imports decisions ($Q_1(P)$), as well as sales at the other nodes of the network."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Local allocation component of the utility-integrated model for Coalition {VIU, Private investor}, whose distribution constraints are also included in the grand-coalition model. | Local microgrid allocation model for Coalition {Private investor, D}. | Microgrid allocation optimization in Coalition {Private investor, D}, within the iterative utility–microgrid equilibrium calculation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g04-E12","v141-b-g04-E16","v141-b-g04-E21","v141-b-g04-E25","v141-b-g05-e07"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E25","v141-b-g05-e07"]},"paper_scope_note":"Different alliances and fixed-point steps are retained separately; the original text explicitly states that convergence is not guaranteed, and price feedback cannot be described as having guaranteed equilibrium."}});
